This tree is a fork of Neroued/ninfer at commit feaf4dd. The modifications add
tensor-parallel execution across two GPUs and YaRN positional scaling for
1,048,576-token contexts to the 27B execution package. They touch, in summary:

  * src/core           two-device ExecutionContext; per-device arenas, streams
                       and graph objects; per-device memoization of kernel
                       attribute opt-ins
  * src/ops            allreduce_sum and allgather collectives; column- and
                       row-parallel split forms of the nine Op families that
                       carry sharded weights; a 12-Q-head/2-KV-head GQA
                       geometry; a YaRN frequency-buffer rope kernel; a
                       1,048,576-key visible-key domain and the shared-memory
                       accounting that goes with it
  * src/artifact       sharded weight and shard plans, and the materialization
                       that binds a shard of a tensor to one device
  * src/targets        two-rank Program wiring: split prefill, decode, MTP and
                       output-head schedules; cross-device graph capture and
                       replay; peer state publication
  * src/runtime,       --tp / --devices / --rope / --yarn-* plumbing through the
    src/serve, apps    public Engine, the CLI and the server
  * eval/, tools/tp2/  1M needle, soak and power runners; P2P, capture and
                       transport probes; the tp1-to-tp2 parity harness; the
                       vLLM YaRN reference dumper
  * tests/, scripts/   split-Op oracles, dual-device integration and graph
                       tests, the YaRN drift guard, and the tp1 golden-token
                       identity gate against upstream feaf4dd

That upstream TP2 revision preserved single-GPU (--tp 1) behaviour from
feaf4dd; see tests/data/tp1-golden/MANIFEST.md for its token-level comparison.
Those measurements do not qualify the later Volta execution paths below.

Volta and V100X2 modifications
-----------------------------
This fork incorporates Volta CUDA kernels and build support from
https://github.com/geoffwatts/ninfer-v100, distributed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

The V100X2 integration at https://github.com/tuxKOH/ninfer-V100X2 combines
that work with the RTX 3060 TP2 branch. It adds preserved GGUF Q4_K/Q6_K
artifact conversion and execution, Volta long-context INT8 attention,
verified two-device transport, and the corresponding validation and tools.
The integration is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The SM70 TP2/TP4 packet-push collectives in src/ops/kernel/allreduce.cuh use
the two-epoch/sentinel transport design from 1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM's
csrc/custom_all_reduce.cuh, which credits haohervchb/sglang-V100 for its
one-shot push collective. Both projects distribute that implementation
under Apache-2.0. This adaptation uses BF16 packets, keeps the local
contribution in registers, and has fixed per-Program startup storage. TP4
uses separate source channels and a fixed global-rank FP32 summation order.

The TP4 long-attention direct split combine also uses 1Cat's grouped-attention
combine as a design reference. This adaptation retains NInfer's packed INT8
group-64 KV, BF16 partials, FP32 split summation order and denominator.

The TP4 wide-message reduce-scatter/allgather in src/ops/common/allreduce.cu
uses 1Cat's cross_device_reduce_2stage as a reference. Projection epilogues in
src/ops/linear_add/nvfp4 publish represented BF16 contributions directly to
the same packet mailboxes before the fused sum/RMSNorm consumer. These
adaptations preserve fixed global-rank FP32 summation and one BF16 sum store.

The SM70 D256 Split-D prefill implementation in
src/ops/launcher/gqa_attention_volta_splitd.cu adapts the core of 1Cat-vLLM's
csrc/attention/sm70_v37/tail.cu (Copyright 2026 1CatAI, Apache-2.0). Its MMA
layout and online-softmax helpers derive from zhinianqin/flash-attention-v100,
revision c2eda5e6115b98c3ba4bfd181570668742eece22, csrc/flash_attn/src/{utils,
kernel_traits,softmax,mask}.h (Copyright 2023-2024 Tri Dao, BSD-3-Clause).
The complete BSD license and authors are retained under
third_party/flash_attention_sm70/. NInfer supplies native buffers, explicit
causal positions, padded tails and the original INT8/BF16 cache boundaries.

Model artifacts
---------------
The published artifacts are derived from Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B, Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B and
Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B. Their NVFP4 profiles also use the fixed packed weights from
rdtand/Qwen3.6-27B-PrismaSCOUT-Blackwell-NVFP4-BF16-vllm and
unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4. Those source repositories are distributed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Vendored dependencies retain their own license files under third_party/.

CPU visual encoding uses BLAS (OpenBLAS in the Linux prebuilt package), BSD 3-Clause.
Copyright (c) 2011-2014, The OpenBLAS Project. License: third_party/licenses/OpenBLAS.txt.

Structured output statically links the C++ core of XGrammar v0.2.8
(https://github.com/mlc-ai/xgrammar), Copyright (c) 2024 by XGrammar Contributors,
Apache License, Version 2.0, with its picojson (BSD 2-Clause) and DLPack (Apache-2.0)
headers. The sources are fetched at configure time and are not modified.
